## 3. CORE CONCEPTS & TERMINOLOGY

| Term | Meaning | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| **Schema** | Contract between client and server — defines all types, queries, mutations | The "blueprint" of your API |
| **Type** | A shape of data with specific fields | `User { id, name, email }` |
| **Field** | A single piece of data on a type | `name`, `email` |
| **Query** | Read operation — fetching data | `{ user(id: 1) { name } }` |
| **Mutation** | Write operation — creating/updating/deleting | `mutation { createUser(name: "John") }` |
| **Subscription** | Real-time operation — push data to client | `subscription { messageAdded { text } }` |
| **Resolver** | Function that returns data for a specific field | `resolvers.Query.user = (_, { id }) => db.findUser(id)` |
| **Argument** | Parameter passed to a field | `user(id: 1)` — `id` is an argument |
| **Variable** | Dynamic values passed separately from query | `$id: ID!` |
| **Fragment** | Reusable set of fields | `fragment UserFields on User { name email }` |
| **Alias** | Rename a field in the response | `johnUser: user(id: 1) { name }` |
| **Directive** | Modifier that changes execution | `@include(if: $showEmail)` |
| **Introspection** | Query the schema itself | `{ __schema { types { name } } }` |
| **SDL** | Schema Definition Language — syntax for defining schema | `type User { name: String! }` |
| **Root Types** | Entry points — Query, Mutation, Subscription | `type Query { ... }` |
| **Input Type** | Special type for mutation arguments | `input CreateUserInput { name: String! }` |
| **Enum** | Set of allowed values | `enum Role { ADMIN USER GUEST }` |
| **Interface** | Abstract type with shared fields | `interface Node { id: ID! }` |
| **Union** | Type that can be one of several types | `union SearchResult = User \| Post` |
| **Non-Null** | Field that can never be null | `name: String!` (the `!` means required) |
| **List** | Array of items | `posts: [Post!]!` |

