## 6. OBJECT TYPES & FIELDS

### Defining Types
```graphql
type User {
  # Scalar fields
  id: ID!                    # Required unique identifier
  name: String!              # Required string
  email: String!             # Required string
  age: Int                   # Optional integer (can be null)
  isActive: Boolean!         # Required boolean
  balance: Float             # Optional float
  
  # Relationship fields
  posts: [Post!]!            # Required list of non-null Posts
  friends: [User!]           # Optional list of non-null Users
  profile: Profile           # Optional single Profile
  
  # Field with arguments
  posts(limit: Int = 10, offset: Int = 0): [Post!]!
  
  # Computed field
  fullName: String!          # Resolved by a custom resolver
  postCount: Int!            # Resolved by counting posts
}
```

### Type Relationships
```graphql
# One-to-One
type User {
  profile: Profile           # User has ONE Profile
}
type Profile {
  user: User!                # Profile belongs to ONE User
}

# One-to-Many
type User {
  posts: [Post!]!            # User has MANY Posts
}
type Post {
  author: User!              # Post belongs to ONE User
}

# Many-to-Many
type Post {
  tags: [Tag!]!              # Post has MANY Tags
}
type Tag {
  posts: [Post!]!            # Tag has MANY Posts
}
```

