## 7. QUERIES — READING DATA

### Basic Query
```graphql
# Simple field query
query {
  user(id: "1") {
    name
    email
  }
}

# Response:
{
  "data": {
    "user": {
      "name": "John Doe",
      "email": "john@example.com"
    }
  }
}
```

### Nested Query (Related Data)
```graphql
query {
  user(id: "1") {
    name
    email
    posts {
      title
      content
      comments {
        text
        author {
          name
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

# Response:
{
  "data": {
    "user": {
      "name": "John Doe",
      "email": "john@example.com",
      "posts": [
        {
          "title": "My First Post",
          "content": "Hello World!",
          "comments": [
            {
              "text": "Great post!",
              "author": {
                "name": "Jane Smith"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### Multiple Root Queries in One Request
```graphql
query {
  user(id: "1") {
    name
  }
  posts {
    title
  }
  totalUsers
}

# All three queries execute in ONE HTTP request
```

### Named Queries (Best Practice)
```graphql
# Always name your queries in production
query GetUserProfile {
  user(id: "1") {
    name
    email
  }
}

query GetAllPosts {
  posts {
    title
    author {
      name
    }
  }
}

query GetDashboardData {
  me {
    name
    role
  }
  recentPosts(limit: 5) {
    title
    createdAt
  }
  stats {
    totalUsers
    totalPosts
  }
}
```

