## 9. SUBSCRIPTIONS — REAL-TIME DATA

### How Subscriptions Work
```
1. Client opens a WebSocket connection to /graphql
2. Client sends a subscription query
3. Server pushes data through WebSocket whenever an event occurs
4. Connection stays open until client unsubscribes
```

### Schema Definition
```graphql
type Subscription {
  # Triggered when any new post is created
  postCreated: Post!
  
  # Triggered when a comment is added to a specific post
  commentAdded(postId: ID!): Comment!
  
  # Triggered when a user comes online/offline
  userStatusChanged: User!
  
  # Triggered on new messages in a chat room
  messageSent(roomId: ID!): Message!
}
```

### Client Usage (Apollo Client)
```javascript
import { useSubscription, gql } from '@apollo/client';

const NEW_COMMENT = gql`
  subscription OnCommentAdded($postId: ID!) {
    commentAdded(postId: $postId) {
      id
      text
      author {
        name
      }
      createdAt
    }
  }
`;

function Comments({ postId }) {
  const { data, loading, error } = useSubscription(NEW_COMMENT, {
    variables: { postId },
  });

  if (data) {
    console.log('New comment:', data.commentAdded);
  }

  return <div>{/* render comments */}</div>;
}
```

### Server Implementation (Apollo Server with subscriptions)
```javascript
import { PubSub } from 'graphql-subscriptions';

const pubsub = new PubSub();
const COMMENT_ADDED = 'COMMENT_ADDED';

const resolvers = {
  Mutation: {
    addComment: async (_, { postId, text }, context) => {
      const comment = await Comment.create({ postId, text, authorId: context.user.id });
      
      // Publish event
      pubsub.publish(COMMENT_ADDED, { 
        commentAdded: comment,
        postId 
      });
      
      return comment;
    },
  },
  Subscription: {
    commentAdded: {
      subscribe: (_, { postId }) => {
        // Filter: only send events for this specific post
        return pubsub.asyncIterator(COMMENT_ADDED);
      },
      resolve: (payload) => payload.commentAdded,
    },
  },
};
```

