## 10. ARGUMENTS & VARIABLES

### Arguments in Schema
```graphql
type Query {
  # Required argument
  user(id: ID!): User
  
  # Optional argument
  users(role: Role): [User!]!
  
  # Multiple arguments
  posts(status: PostStatus, limit: Int = 10, offset: Int = 0): [Post!]!
  
  # Complex arguments with input type
  searchPosts(filter: PostFilterInput!, pagination: PaginationInput): PostConnection!
}
```

### Arguments in Queries
```graphql
# Inline arguments
query {
  user(id: "123") {
    name
  }
  posts(status: PUBLISHED, limit: 5) {
    title
  }
}
```

### Variables (Dynamic Values)
```graphql
# Query with variable declarations
query GetUser($userId: ID!, $includeEmail: Boolean = false) {
  user(id: $userId) {
    name
    email @include(if: $includeEmail)
    posts {
      title
    }
  }
}
```

**Variables JSON (sent with the query):**
```json
{
  "userId": "123",
  "includeEmail": true
}
```

### Variable Types
```graphql
# Required scalar
$id: ID!

# Optional scalar
$name: String

# Required input type
$input: CreateUserInput!

# Required list
$ids: [ID!]!

# Optional with default
$limit: Int = 10

# Enum
$role: Role = USER
```

### Full Request Structure (HTTP POST body)
```json
{
  "query": "query GetUser($id: ID!) { user(id: $id) { name email } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": "123"
  },
  "operationName": "GetUser"
}
```

