## 11. FRAGMENTS

Fragments let you **reuse sets of fields** across multiple queries.

### Basic Fragment
```graphql
# Define fragment
fragment UserBasicInfo on User {
  id
  name
  email
  role
}

# Use in queries
query {
  user(id: "1") {
    ...UserBasicInfo
    posts {
      title
    }
  }
  me {
    ...UserBasicInfo
    isActive
  }
}

# Equivalent to writing:
query {
  user(id: "1") {
    id
    name
    email
    role
    posts {
      title
    }
  }
  me {
    id
    name
    email
    role
    isActive
  }
}
```

### Nested Fragments
```graphql
fragment PostSummary on Post {
  id
  title
  status
  createdAt
}

fragment PostWithAuthor on Post {
  ...PostSummary
  content
  author {
    ...UserBasicInfo
  }
}

fragment UserWithPosts on User {
  ...UserBasicInfo
  posts {
    ...PostSummary
  }
}

query GetDashboard {
  me {
    ...UserWithPosts
  }
  latestPosts {
    ...PostWithAuthor
  }
}
```

### Inline Fragments (for Unions/Interfaces)
```graphql
query Search($query: String!) {
  search(query: $query) {
    # Common fields from interface
    ... on Node {
      id
      createdAt
    }
    # Type-specific fields
    ... on User {
      name
      email
    }
    ... on Post {
      title
      content
    }
    ... on Comment {
      text
    }
  }
}
```

### __typename (Type Discrimination)
```graphql
query Search($query: String!) {
