## 12. ALIASES

Aliases let you **rename fields** in the response — essential when querying the same field with different arguments.

```graphql
# Without aliases (ERROR — duplicate field "user")
query {
  user(id: "1") { name }     # ← Can't have two "user" fields
  user(id: "2") { name }     # ← Conflict!
}

# With aliases (WORKS)
query {
  firstUser: user(id: "1") {
    name
  }
  secondUser: user(id: "2") {
    name
  }
}

# Response:
{
  "data": {
    "firstUser": {
      "name": "Alice"
    },
    "secondUser": {
      "name": "Bob"
    }
  }
}
```

### Practical Example — Dashboard
```graphql
query Dashboard {
  publishedPosts: posts(status: PUBLISHED) {
    title
    likes
  }
  draftPosts: posts(status: DRAFT) {
    title
    createdAt
  }
  archivedCount: postsCount(status: ARCHIVED)
  publishedCount: postsCount(status: PUBLISHED)
}
```

