## 16. UNION TYPES

A union means a type can be **one of several types** (no shared fields required).

```graphql
# Union definition
union SearchResult = User | Post | Comment

union Media = Image | Video | Audio

union NotificationTarget = User | Team | Channel

# Usage in schema
type Query {
  search(query: String!): [SearchResult!]!
}

# Client query — MUST use inline fragments
query Search($q: String!) {
  search(query: $q) {
    __typename        # "User", "Post", or "Comment"
    
    ... on User {
      id
      name
      email
    }
    
    ... on Post {
      id
      title
      content
      author {
        name
      }
    }
    
    ... on Comment {
      id
      text
    }
  }
}

# Response:
{
  "data": {
    "search": [
      { "__typename": "User", "id": "1", "name": "John", "email": "john@test.com" },
      { "__typename": "Post", "id": "5", "title": "GraphQL Guide", "content": "...", "author": { "name": "Jane" } },
      { "__typename": "Comment", "id": "10", "text": "Great article!" }
    ]
  }
}
```

### Interface vs Union

| Interface | Union |
|-----------|-------|
| Types share common fields | Types have NO common fields required |
| `interface Node { id: ID! }` | `union Result = A \| B \| C` |
| Types MUST implement all interface fields | Types are independent |
| Good for: things that share a structure | Good for: search results, mixed feeds |

