## 22. PAGINATION

### Offset-Based Pagination
```graphql
# Schema
type Query {
  posts(page: Int = 1, limit: Int = 10): PostPage!
}

type PostPage {
  data: [Post!]!
  totalCount: Int!
  currentPage: Int!
  totalPages: Int!
  hasMore: Boolean!
}

# Query
query {
  posts(page: 2, limit: 10) {
    data {
      title
      author { name }
    }
    totalCount
    currentPage
    totalPages
    hasMore
  }
}
```

### Cursor-Based Pagination (Relay Style — Recommended)
```graphql
# Schema (Relay specification)
type Query {
  posts(first: Int, after: String, last: Int, before: String): PostConnection!
}

type PostConnection {
  edges: [PostEdge!]!
  pageInfo: PageInfo!
  totalCount: Int!
}

type PostEdge {
  cursor: String!      # Opaque cursor (usually base64-encoded ID)
  node: Post!          # The actual data
}

type PageInfo {
  hasNextPage: Boolean!
  hasPreviousPage: Boolean!
  startCursor: String
  endCursor: String
}

# Query — get first 10 posts
query {
  posts(first: 10) {
    edges {
      cursor
      node {
        title
        createdAt
      }
    }
    pageInfo {
      hasNextPage
      endCursor
    }
    totalCount
  }
}

# Query — get next 10 posts after a cursor
query {
  posts(first: 10, after: "Y3Vyc29yXzEw") {
    edges {
      cursor
      node {
        title
      }
    }
    pageInfo {
      hasNextPage
      endCursor
    }
  }
}
```

### Resolver for Cursor Pagination
```javascript
const resolvers = {
  Query: {
    posts: async (_, { first = 10, after }, context) => {
      let query = {};
      
      if (after) {
        const cursorId = Buffer.from(after, 'base64').toString('utf-8');
        query._id = { $gt: cursorId };
      }
      
      const posts = await context.db.posts
        .find(query)
        .sort({ _id: 1 })
        .limit(first + 1);  // Fetch one extra to check hasNextPage
      
      const hasNextPage = posts.length > first;
      const edges = posts.slice(0, first).map(post => ({
        cursor: Buffer.from(post.id.toString()).toString('base64'),
        node: post,
      }));
      
      const totalCount = await context.db.posts.countDocuments();
      
      return {
        edges,
        totalCount,
        pageInfo: {
          hasNextPage,
          hasPreviousPage: !!after,
          startCursor: edges[0]?.cursor,
          endCursor: edges[edges.length - 1]?.cursor,
        },
      };
    },
  },
};
```

### Offset vs Cursor Pagination

| Aspect | Offset | Cursor |
|--------|--------|--------|
| Simplicity | Simple (`page`, `limit`) | More complex |
| Performance | Slow on large datasets | Fast (indexed) |
| Consistency | Items can shift between pages | Stable — no duplicates |
| Use case | Admin dashboards, small datasets | Feeds, infinite scroll, large datasets |
| Standard | No standard | Relay spec (widely adopted) |

