## 26. SECURITY BEST PRACTICES

### 1. Query Depth Limiting
```javascript
// Prevent deeply nested queries that overload the server
import depthLimit from 'graphql-depth-limit';

const server = new ApolloServer({
  typeDefs,
  resolvers,
  validationRules: [depthLimit(7)], // Max depth of 7
});

// This would be rejected (too deep):
query {
  user {                    # depth 1
    posts {                 # depth 2
      comments {            # depth 3
        author {            # depth 4
          posts {            # depth 5
            comments {       # depth 6
              author {       # depth 7
                posts { }    # depth 8 — REJECTED!
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### 2. Query Complexity Analysis
```javascript
import { createComplexityLimitRule } from 'graphql-validation-complexity';

const server = new ApolloServer({
  typeDefs,
  resolvers,
  validationRules: [
    createComplexityLimitRule(1000), // Max complexity score
  ],
});

// In schema, assign costs:
type Query {
  users: [User!]! @complexity(value: 10)      # Each user costs 10
  posts: [Post!]! @complexity(value: 5)       # Each post costs 5
}
```

### 3. Rate Limiting
```javascript
import rateLimit from 'express-rate-limit';

// Apply to /graphql endpoint
app.use('/graphql', rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 100,                  // 100 requests per window
  message: 'Too many requests',
}));
```

### 4. Disable Introspection in Production
```javascript
const server = new ApolloServer({
  typeDefs,
  resolvers,
  introspection: process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production',
});
```

### 5. Input Validation
```javascript
const resolvers = {
  Mutation: {
    createUser: async (_, { input }) => {
      // Validate input
      if (input.name.length > 100) throw new Error('Name too long');
      if (!/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(input.email)) {
        throw new Error('Invalid email');
      }
      // ...
    },
  },
};
```

### 6. Field-Level Authorization
```javascript
const resolvers = {
  User: {
    email: (parent, _, context) => {
      // Only show email to the user themselves or admins
      if (context.user?.id === parent.id || context.user?.role === 'ADMIN') {
        return parent.email;
      }
      return null;
    },
    
    salary: (parent, _, context) => {
      if (context.user?.role !== 'ADMIN') {
        throw new GraphQLError('Not authorized', {
          extensions: { code: 'FORBIDDEN' },
        });
      }
      return parent.salary;
    },
  },
};
```

### 7. Persisted Queries (Allowlisting)
```javascript
// Only allow pre-registered queries
const server = new ApolloServer({
  typeDefs,
  resolvers,
  persistedQueries: {
    // Only registered query hashes are allowed
    cache: new KeyvAdapter(new Keyv()),
  },
});
```

### Security Checklist
```
□ Authentication (JWT / OAuth / Session)
□ Authorization (role-based in resolvers)
□ Query depth limiting
□ Query complexity analysis
□ Rate limiting
□ Input validation / sanitization
□ Disable introspection in production
□ Persisted queries (optional)
□ HTTPS only
□ CORS configuration
□ Error masking (don't leak internal errors)
□ Timeout limits on queries
□ Logging & monitoring
```

