## 36. FEDERATION & MICROSERVICES

### What is GraphQL Federation?
Federation lets you compose a **single graph from multiple services** — each team owns their part of the schema.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  APOLLO GATEWAY                      │
│              (Single /graphql endpoint)              │
├─────────────┬──────────────┬────────────────────────┤
│   Users     │    Posts     │     Comments            │
│  Service    │   Service    │     Service             │
│  (team A)   │   (team B)   │     (team C)            │
│             │              │                         │
│ type User   │ type Post    │ type Comment            │
│   id        │   id         │   id                    │
│   name      │   title      │   text                  │
│   email     │   author     │   author                │
└─────────────┴──────────────┴────────────────────────┘
```

### Subgraph: Users Service
```graphql
# Users subgraph
extend schema @link(url: "https://specs.apollo.dev/federation/v2.0", import: ["@key"])

type Query {
  users: [User!]!
  user(id: ID!): User
}

type User @key(fields: "id") {
  id: ID!
  name: String!
  email: String!
}
```

### Subgraph: Posts Service
```graphql
# Posts subgraph
extend schema @link(url: "https://specs.apollo.dev/federation/v2.0", import: ["@key", "@external"])

type Query {
  posts: [Post!]!
  post(id: ID!): Post
}

type Post @key(fields: "id") {
  id: ID!
  title: String!
  content: String!
  authorId: ID!
  author: User!
}

# Reference to User from Users service
type User @key(fields: "id", resolvable: false) {
  id: ID!
}
```

### Gateway (Apollo Router)
```yaml
# supergraph.yaml
federation_version: =2.0
subgraphs:
  users:
    routing_url: http://users-service:4001/graphql
    schema:
      subgraph_url: http://users-service:4001/graphql
  posts:
    routing_url: http://posts-service:4002/graphql
    schema:
      subgraph_url: http://posts-service:4002/graphql
```

```bash
# Compose supergraph
rover supergraph compose --config supergraph.yaml > supergraph.graphql

# Start router
./router --supergraph supergraph.graphql
```

