## 38. PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION

### 1. Query Batching
```javascript
// Apollo Client batches multiple queries in a single HTTP request
import { BatchHttpLink } from '@apollo/client/link/batch-http';

const link = new BatchHttpLink({
  uri: '/graphql',
  batchMax: 5,       // Max 5 queries per batch
  batchInterval: 20, // Wait 20ms to collect queries
});
```

### 2. Persisted Queries
```javascript
// Send query hash instead of full query string
import { createPersistedQueryLink } from '@apollo/client/link/persisted-queries';
import { sha256 } from 'crypto-hash';

const link = createPersistedQueryLink({ sha256 }).concat(httpLink);

// First request: sends hash + full query
// Subsequent requests: sends only hash (much smaller payload)
```

### 3. Automatic Persisted Queries (APQ)
```
First request:
  Client → "hash: abc123" → Server
  Server: "I don't know hash abc123" → 404
  Client → "hash: abc123 + full query" → Server
  Server: stores { abc123: "query { users { name } }" }

All future requests:
  Client → "hash: abc123" → Server
  Server: executes stored query → response
  (Much smaller payload!)
```

### 4. Defer and Stream (@defer, @stream)
```graphql
# @defer — load parts of query later
query {
  user(id: "1") {
    name
    email
    ... @defer {         # This part arrives later
      posts {
        title
        comments {
          text
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

# @stream — stream list items one by one
query {
  posts @stream(initialCount: 5) {    # First 5 arrive immediately
    title                              # Rest stream in
    author { name }
  }
}
```

### 5. Field-Level Caching
```javascript
// Cache control per field
const typePolicies = {
  User: {
    fields: {
      posts: {
        // Cache posts for each user separately
        keyArgs: ['status'],
        merge(existing = [], incoming) {
          return [...existing, ...incoming];
        },
      },
    },
  },
};
```

### 6. Avoid N+1 with DataLoader (see Section 21)

### Performance Checklist
```
□ Use DataLoader for relationship fields
□ Implement pagination (don't fetch unlimited lists)
□ Set query depth limits
□ Set query complexity limits
□ Use persisted queries in production
□ Enable response caching (CDN, server-side)
□ Use @defer for non-critical data
□ Batch multiple queries
□ Monitor query performance (Apollo Studio)
□ Index database fields used in resolvers
□ Use projections (only select needed DB columns)
```

