## QUICK REFERENCE CHEAT SHEET

### Query Syntax
```graphql
query OperationName($var: Type!) {        # Named query with variable
  fieldName(arg: $var) {                   # Field with argument
    scalarField                            # Return scalar
    objectField { nestedField }            # Return nested object
    ...FragmentName                        # Spread fragment
    aliasName: fieldName(arg: value)       # Alias
    conditionalField @include(if: $flag)   # Directive
  }
}
```

### Type System
```graphql
# Object type
type User { name: String! }

# Input type (for arguments)
input CreateUserInput { name: String! }

# Enum
enum Role { ADMIN USER }

# Interface
interface Node { id: ID! }

# Union
union Result = User | Post

# Custom scalar
scalar DateTime

# Nullability
String     → nullable
String!    → non-null
[String!]! → non-null list of non-null strings
```

### Key Annotations
```graphql
@deprecated(reason: "Use X instead")  # Mark field deprecated
@include(if: $bool)                   # Conditionally include
@skip(if: $bool)                      # Conditionally skip
@key(fields: "id")                    # Federation entity key
@cacheControl(maxAge: 300)            # Cache hint
```

### Apollo Client Hooks
```javascript
useQuery(QUERY, { variables, fetchPolicy, skip })
useLazyQuery(QUERY)     → [executeQuery, { data, loading }]
useMutation(MUTATION)   → [mutate, { data, loading, error }]
useSubscription(SUB)    → { data, loading, error }
```

### HTTP Request Format
```
POST /graphql
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
  "query": "query { users { id name } }",
  "variables": { "id": "1" },
  "operationName": "GetUsers"
}
```

### Response Format
```json
{
  "data": { "users": [{ "id": "1", "name": "Alice" }] },
  "errors": [],
  "extensions": {}
}
```
